Package: shani-chronoa
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, python3-httpx, espeak-ng, pipewire, wireplumber, libnotify-bin, upower, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng, bubblewrap, libsecret, psmisc, i2c-tools, policykit-1, bluez, pciutils, usbutils, smartmontools, power-profiles-daemon, udisks2, cups-client, sane-utils, nmap, network-manager
# The TTS chain is piper, rhvoice, espeak-ng, and kokoro only when the user asks for it
# (kokoro-tts-enabled, default false - real-time factor 1.2). Kokoro, like Piper, is a
# pinned download into the user's home from setup (sherpa-onnx bundles onnxruntime).
# sox is the timbre pass tts.py applies to whichever engine produced the WAV: pitch,
# tempo and rate. Optional like every other optional engine - without it the reply is
# spoken unchanged and the reason is said rather than guessed at.
Suggests: soundtouch, rubberband (higher-quality pitch transposition for singing.py; without them a pitch shift falls back to sox), whisper.cpp (voice input (speech recognition) and the wake phrase), piper-tts (a better TTS voice; espeak-ng is used when absent), sox (voice pitch plus the tempo and rate controls in Settings), python3-mcp, translate-shell, gir1.2-webkit-6.0 (the in-app browser and attaching a page to the conversation), python3-onnxruntime (remove_background for any object, not only people)
Maintainer: Shrinivas Vishnu Kumbhar <shrinivas.v.kumbhar@gmail.com>
Description: Local AI assistant with privacy-first design, integrated into Shanios
 Shani Chronoa is a local-first AI assistant for the Shanios ecosystem.
 It provides speech-to-text via whisper.cpp, LLM inference through Ollama,
 and text-to-speech via Piper TTS, all with a GTK4 GUI interface.
 All processing happens locally ensuring complete privacy and data sovereignty.
